Backport of wolfSSL PR #11986 (https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssl/pull/11986,
commit eb440a49b71c) onto v5.9.4-stable with our other patches applied.

- Load 32-bit stack parameters as 32-bit in the Windows x64 assembly
  (fixes the ChaCha20-Poly1305 <= 64-byte crash and the same bug in
  ML-KEM, FrodoKEM, ML-DSA, SHA-2, X25519 and the AVX-512 kernels).
- Regenerate chacha_encrypt_x64 in chacha_asm.asm, which used the Win64
  argument registers r8/r9 for ChaCha state (wrong output and a bad tail
  pointer on AVX-512VL CPUs).
- chacha.c: only let AVX-512VL steer short input when that kernel is built.
- Add CPUID_SLOW_VAES / CPUID_SLOW_AVX2_SHA3 tuning bits, set on Arrow
  Lake and Lunar Lake, so AES skips VAES and SHA-3/ML-DSA skip the AVX2
  Keccak block there.

Dropped from the backport: the LMS/XMSS hunks in sha256_asm.S,
sha3_asm.S and sha3_asm.asm (those functions are not in 5.9.4),
tests/unit-mcdc and .wolfssl_known_macro_extras.

